Subject: [PATCH] Support large signed HTTP bodies with compatible IPC framing

Keep the existing 16-bit frames unchanged for small requests. Extended XSTS
requests use type 0x8005, the 0xffff marker and a bounded 32-bit payload length.
Reject oversized, malformed and truncated frames before dispatch. The existing
response type remains 6. A paired runtime is required for large requests.

Allow a service socket directory override without changing desktop or audio
state. Exercise both framing variants in the account-free service fixture;
its large request verifies the complete 100 KB body rather than just its size.

